<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Mozart returns two days after his first visit, on the day of his nephrology consultation with Dr. Okonkwo-Brandt. Since starting furosemide each morning he has passed much more urine, and he has lost about a kilogram, but his eyelids are still puffy in the mornings and his ankles swell by evening. The urine is lighter but still brownish. The colicky abdominal pain and vomiting have stopped, the knee and ankle aches are easing, and he has had no fever. He has a mild headache in the mornings, with no change in vision, confusion, chest pain, or breathlessness lying flat. He is taking penicillin twice a day and has stopped ibuprofen. He is keeping salt low and drinking about a liter and a half a day. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Swelling</td><td>Less, but still puffy eyelids and ankles</td></tr><tr><td>Urine</td><td>More urine; color lighter but brownish</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>63.0 kg, from 64.2</td></tr><tr><td>Joints</td><td>Aches easing; no swollen joints</td></tr><tr><td>Red flags</td><td>No vision change, confusion, chest pain, or orthopnea</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
